      "langs": {
        "id": {
          "title": "Nasionalisasi Minyak Meksiko (1938)",
          "desc": "Nasionalisasi Minyak Meksiko (1938)",
          "content": "<p class=\"mb-4\">Pada akhir abad ke-19, Lázaro Cárdenas memperluas pemerintahan terpusat dan menjanjikan stabilitas setelah puluhan tahun konflik. Rezim ini bertahan lama melalui pemilu yang dikendalikan dan jaringan politik.</p><p class=\"mb-4\">Pemerintahannya membangun rel kereta, telegraf, tambang, serta investasi asing yang mempercepat modernisasi. Namun pertumbuhan tersebut terkonsentrasi di kota dan sektor elite, sementara banyak petani kehilangan tanah dan pekerja menghadapi kondisi keras.</p><p class=\"mb-4\">Ketimpangan, represi, dan penuaan kepemimpinan memicu oposisi yang akhirnya meledak dalam Revolusi Meksiko. Warisan periodenya tetap diperdebatkan karena modernisasi fisik berjalan berdampingan dengan biaya sosial yang besar.</p>",
          "source": "Britannica",
          "sourceUrl": "https://www.britannica.com/place/Mexico",
          "sourceSnippet": "Britannica — Mexico",
          "source2": "Library of Congress",
          "sourceUrl2": "https://www.loc.gov/collections/",
          "sourceSnippet2": "Library of Congress — Mexico",
          "source3": "INEHRM Mexico",
          "sourceUrl3": "https://www.inehrm.gob.mx/",
          "sourceSnippet3": "INEHRM — Historical Research"
        },
        "en": {
          "title": "Mexico’s Oil Nationalization (1938)",
          "desc": "Mexico’s Oil Nationalization (1938)",
          "content": "<p class=\"mb-4\">In the late nineteenth century, Lázaro Cárdenas expanded central government and promised stability after decades of conflict. The regime lasted through controlled elections and political networks.</p><p class=\"mb-4\">His government built railways, telegraphs, mines, and foreign investment that accelerated modernization. Yet growth was concentrated in cities and elite sectors, while many farmers lost land and workers faced harsh conditions.</p><p class=\"mb-4\">Inequality, repression, and an aging leadership fueled opposition that eventually exploded into the Mexican Revolution. Its legacy remains debated because physical modernization came with major social costs.</p>",
          "source": "Britannica",
          "sourceUrl": "https://www.britannica.com/place/Mexico",
          "sourceSnippet": "Britannica — Mexico",
          "source2": "Library of Congress",
          "sourceUrl2": "https://www.loc.gov/collections/",
          "sourceSnippet2": "Library of Congress — Mexico",
          "source3": "INEHRM Mexico",
          "sourceUrl3": "https://www.inehrm.gob.mx/",
          "sourceSnippet3": "INEHRM — Historical Research"
        },
        "ja": {
          "title": "メキシコ石油国有化（1938年）",
          "desc": "メキシコ石油国有化（1938年）",
          "content": "<p class=\"mb-4\">19世紀末、Lázaro Cárdenasは長年の紛争後に中央集権と安定を拡大しました。政権は管理された選挙と政治網で長く続きました。</p><p class=\"mb-4\">鉄道、電信、鉱山、外国投資が近代化を進めましたが、成長は都市とエリートに集中し、多くの農民が土地を失いました。</p><p class=\"mb-4\">格差と弾圧、指導者の高齢化への反発がメキシコ革命を招きました。物理的近代化と大きな社会的犠牲が併存した時代です。</p>",
          "source": "Britannica",
          "sourceUrl": "https://www.britannica.com/place/Mexico",
          "sourceSnippet": "Britannica — Mexico",
          "source2": "Library of Congress",
          "sourceUrl2": "https://www.loc.gov/collections/",
          "sourceSnippet2": "Library of Congress — Mexico",
          "source3": "INEHRM Mexico",
          "sourceUrl3": "https://www.inehrm.gob.mx/",
          "sourceSnippet3": "INEHRM — Historical Research"
        },
        "ko": {
          "title": "멕시코 석유 국유화(1938년)",
          "desc": "멕시코 석유 국유화(1938년)",
          "content": "<p class=\"mb-4\">19세기 말 Lázaro Cárdenas은 수십 년 분쟁 뒤 중앙정부와 안정을 확대했습니다. 정권은 통제된 선거와 정치 네트워크로 오래 유지되었습니다.</p><p class=\"mb-4\">철도, 전신, 광산과 외국인 투자가 근대화를 가속했지만 성장은 도시와 엘리트에 집중됐고 많은 농민이 토지를 잃었습니다.</p><p class=\"mb-4\">불평등과 탄압, 지도자의 고령화가 멕시코 혁명을 촉발했습니다. 물질적 근대화와 큰 사회적 희생이 함께한 시대였습니다.</p>",
          "source": "Britannica",
          "sourceUrl": "https://www.britannica.com/place/Mexico",
          "sourceSnippet": "Britannica — Mexico",
          "source2": "Library of Congress",
          "sourceUrl2": "https://www.loc.gov/collections/",
          "sourceSnippet2": "Library of Congress — Mexico",
          "source3": "INEHRM Mexico",
          "sourceUrl3": "https://www.inehrm.gob.mx/",
          "sourceSnippet3": "INEHRM — Historical Research"
        },
        "zh": {
          "title": "墨西哥石油国有化（1938年）",
          "desc": "墨西哥石油国有化（1938年）",
          "content": "<p class=\"mb-4\">19世纪末，Lázaro Cárdenas在多年冲突后扩大中央政府并承诺稳定。政权通过受控选举和政治网络长期维持。</p><p class=\"mb-4\">铁路、电报、矿业和外国投资推动现代化，但增长集中在城市和精英，许多农民失去土地。</p><p class=\"mb-4\">不平等、镇压和领导层老化引发反对，最终导致墨西哥革命。现代化与巨大的社会代价并存。</p>",
          "source": "Britannica",
          "sourceUrl": "https://www.britannica.com/place/Mexico",
          "sourceSnippet": "Britannica — Mexico",
          "source2": "Library of Congress",
          "sourceUrl2": "https://www.loc.gov/collections/",
          "sourceSnippet2": "Library of Congress — Mexico",
          "source3": "INEHRM Mexico",
          "sourceUrl3": "https://www.inehrm.gob.mx/",
          "sourceSnippet3": "INEHRM — Historical Research"
        }
      }
